// Service boundaries today vs target (cloud-architecture-diagram)
// Why it is safe to build commerce before the split: order-service depends on
// the catalogue contract, never on the database. See order-service/SYSTEM_DESIGN.md.

title Service Split - Today vs Target

Today [color: gray] {
  BackendNow [icon: nodejs, label: "backend :5000 - User + auth + Course + Enrollment + Video + presign"]
  TranscoderNow [icon: nodejs, label: "video-transcoder - callback only, dead Prisma client"]
  NotifyNow [icon: java, label: "notification-service - scaffold"]
  OrderNow [icon: java, label: "order-service - scaffold only"]
  DbNow [icon: postgresql, label: "Postgres public - one Prisma schema, two copies"]
}

Target [color: blue] {
  AuthSvc [icon: nodejs, label: "auth-service - User, tokens, OTP"]
  CourseSvc [icon: nodejs, label: "course-service - Course, Enrollment, Video"]
  OrderSvc [icon: java, label: "order-service - Order, Payment, Refund"]
  NotifySvc [icon: java, label: "notification-service - all outbound messages"]
  TranscoderSvc [icon: nodejs, label: "video-transcoder - callback only, no Prisma"]
  AuthDb [icon: postgresql, label: "schema auth"]
  CourseDb [icon: postgresql, label: "schema course"]
  OrderDb [icon: postgresql, label: "schema orders - Flyway"]
  NotifyDb [icon: mongodb, label: "Mongo notifications"]
}

BackendNow > DbNow
TranscoderNow > BackendNow: processed callback
OrderNow > BackendNow: GET /internal/courses/:id
NotifyNow > OrderNow: notifications topic

AuthSvc > AuthDb
CourseSvc > CourseDb
OrderSvc > OrderDb
NotifySvc > NotifyDb
OrderSvc > CourseSvc: GET /internal/courses/:id - unchanged contract
CourseSvc > OrderSvc: consumes order.paid
TranscoderSvc > CourseSvc: processed callback - one base-URL change
AuthSvc > NotifySvc: notifications topic
OrderSvc > NotifySvc: notifications topic

Today > Target: move Course + Enrollment + Video out; order-service changes by zero lines
